{
 "title": "E4XT cord-scaling and envelope measurements, 2026-09-14/15",
 "device": "E4XT Ultra, EOS 4.70",
 "why_this_file": "The raw captures lived in a session temp directory that does not survive a reboot. These are the reduced rows behind RESOLUTION_NOTES 136-144, kept so the fits can be re-derived without re-running the bench. Per-sample envelope tracks are stripped; every row here is a reduced measurement.",
 "subjects": "P009 v0 (tonal, carrier 82.0/164.1/327.4 Hz at notes 52/64/76) and P013 v0 (flat noise, note 24 root-matched). Slot numbers only -- no preset or sample names are recorded anywhere in this file.",
 "detector_notes": "Narrowband: rfft, Hann, power summed over 7 bins, detector bin computed from frequency and FFT size at every call and frozen at the top rung. Floors are measured AT THE SIGNAL BIN with no note sounding -- an argmax over bins finds mains hash and reads ~20 dB high (SS136). Envelope tracks: RMS or narrowband with the window recorded alongside every rise.",
